1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Everyone will tell you temperature
is the creativity dial.

2
00:00:03,625 --> 00:00:06,333
Turn it up for wild, turn
it down for accurate.

3
00:00:06,875 --> 00:00:08,417
That is not what the number does.

4
00:00:08,917 --> 00:00:13,249
One line of arithmetic shows what it
actually controls — and the answer is not

5
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:13,957
truth.

6
00:00:13,958 --> 00:00:16,042
Temperature is a concentration control.

7
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,792
It decides how concentrated the
choice is — not how truthful it is.

8
00:00:21,375 --> 00:00:24,708
Get that backwards, and you will
trust a number for the wrong reason.

9
00:00:24,958 --> 00:00:26,875
Think of the contrast slider on a photo.

10
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:31,707
Slide it up, and bright parts get brighter
and dark parts get darker — everything

11
00:00:31,708 --> 00:00:32,708
pops.

12
00:00:32,917 --> 00:00:36,792
Slide it down, and it all washes
toward the same flat grey.

13
00:00:36,875 --> 00:00:39,583
But the brightest pixel is
still the brightest, either way.

14
00:00:40,083 --> 00:00:41,083
That is temperature.

15
00:00:41,542 --> 00:00:45,125
It changes how much the outcomes
differ — never which one is on top.

16
00:00:45,667 --> 00:00:48,583
And a high-contrast photo is
not a more accurate photo.

17
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:49,833
Here is the whole machine.

18
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:52,292
Three scores — one, two, three.

19
00:00:53,167 --> 00:00:56,666
Exponentiate each one, divide by
the total, and every outcome gets a

20
00:00:56,667 --> 00:00:57,667
probability.

21
00:00:57,917 --> 00:01:03,167
At temperature one those come out to zero
point zero nine, zero point two four, and

22
00:01:03,583 --> 00:01:05,167
zero point six seven.

23
00:01:05,208 --> 00:01:06,208
That is the baseline.

24
00:01:06,875 --> 00:01:11,042
Every number after this is the same three
scores, seen at a different temperature.

25
00:01:11,292 --> 00:01:16,582
So ask the machine the only question that
isolates temperature: what happens to the

26
00:01:16,583 --> 00:01:18,042
ratio between two outcomes?

27
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:20,042
Watch the ratio, not the bars.

28
00:01:20,708 --> 00:01:22,917
Outcome two over outcome zero.

29
00:01:22,958 --> 00:01:26,833
At temperature zero point five
it is fifty-four point six.

30
00:01:26,875 --> 00:01:29,041
At one, seven point three nine.

31
00:01:29,042 --> 00:01:31,667
At two, just two point seven two.

32
00:01:31,708 --> 00:01:34,457
Those are exactly e to the
fourth, e squared, and e.

33
00:01:34,458 --> 00:01:35,1000
Same scores every time.

34
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:38,917
The gap between them is fixed at two.

35
00:01:38,958 --> 00:01:40,167
Only the temperature moved.

36
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,583
Now the limit — what
this does not establish.

37
00:01:43,292 --> 00:01:46,999
Push the temperature down and the best
outcome dominates, but it never becomes

38
00:01:46,1000 --> 00:01:51,958
certain: at zero point one the worst
still holds two times ten to the minus

39
00:01:52,542 --> 00:01:53,166
nine.

40
00:01:53,167 --> 00:01:57,375
Temperature zero is refused outright
— the function raises a value error.

41
00:01:58,250 --> 00:01:59,833
Concentration is not correctness.

42
00:02:00,375 --> 00:02:04,457
Turn the contrast all the way up on a
photo of the wrong person, and all you get

43
00:02:04,458 --> 00:02:06,583
is a sharper picture of the wrong person.

44
00:02:06,833 --> 00:02:07,833
So, one page.

45
00:02:08,417 --> 00:02:13,291
Temperature divides the score gap before
exponentiating, so it rescales every ratio

46
00:02:13,292 --> 00:02:14,292
at once.

47
00:02:14,542 --> 00:02:18,875
The ordering is untouched — outcome two
wins at every temperature we tested.

48
00:02:19,583 --> 00:02:24,125
The sampled counts agree: eight hundred
forty-nine, six hundred thirty, four

49
00:02:24,167 --> 00:02:26,125
hundred sixty-nine, at seed seven.

50
00:02:26,542 --> 00:02:28,958
And none of that is evidence
the answer is right.

51
00:02:29,208 --> 00:02:30,208
Your turn.

52
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:34,707
Here is the prompt: take a softmax over
the scores one, two, three, compute the

53
00:02:34,708 --> 00:02:39,625
ratio of outcome two to outcome zero at
temperatures zero point five, one, and

54
00:02:39,1000 --> 00:02:42,542
two, and check each against
e to the two over T.

55
00:02:43,125 --> 00:02:46,250
Then change only the middle
score and see which ratios move.

56
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:51,333
Run it, and watch which one stays fixed
— that is the identity doing the work.

57
00:02:51,667 --> 00:02:53,958
Temperature is concentration, not truth.

